      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "557058:bfcf2b10-5443-4304-afe6-3aff38ddf271",
           "text": "@Joshua Allan Westgard"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": ":  I would suggest that change the \"l/log-file\"  to \"-l/-log-dir\"  parameter to specify the logs directory which will be logs/ by default.  I don't think there is any need to check in logs directory (I'm not sure that you can check in empty directories in github)",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Also: perhaps we would like to do the same for the csv files? Instead of \"-c/–csv\" option we might have a \"-o/–output-dir\" option where csv files would get dumped.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
