    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:bfcf2b10-5443-4304-afe6-3aff38ddf271",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/JW-4.png",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/JW-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/JW-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/initials/JW-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Joshua Allan Westgard",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Abfcf2b10-5443-4304-afe6-3aff38ddf271",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Thanks, @dbernstein. You're right about checking in empty dirs. The normal workaround is to put a README in it or an empty .gitignore in there, and then github will check it in.  But I would say as long as the code creates the directory if it doesn't exist we don't need to check in the logs directory.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Regarding CSV files, yes, I agree.  It started out as an optional feature, but maybe it should just happen automatically. Also whether or not the CSV always gets created, the -o flag could be used to specify an output directory, and it could just be sent to the logs or to a \"csv\" directory by default.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
